      ":question/math-academy-id": "q-85968",
      ":question/problem": "Suppose that we wish to study the population of shoes in a store. If we choose $10$ blue shoes from the women's section, then which of the following are sources of bias in our sample?\n\n1. All the sampling units are from the same store.\n2. All the sampling units are blue.\n3. All the sampling units are from the women's section."
